 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to seatbelts in a\ntaxi or livery",
    "basePrintNo": "S7623",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7623-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1229-c & 375, V & T L (as proposed in S.7134 & A.8990)",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7623\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to seatbelts in\na taxi or livery\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends the Vehicle and Traffic Law (VTL) to clari-\nfy the intention that liability for a seatbelt infraction committed by a\nminor rests with a parent or guardian when they are present in a vehi-\ncle.\n\nSection 2 of the bill makes a technical amendment.\n\nSection 3 of the bill updates and strengthens the signage required in\nfor-hire vehicles.\n\nSection 4 of the bill directs the Department of Motor Vehicles to under-\ntake a public education campaign for for-hire vehicle drivers and taxi\nand limousine commissions to inform them of their rights and responsi-\nbilities under the new seatbelt law that passed both houses in January\n2020.\n\nSection 5 of the bill is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation makes several technical amendments and enhancements to\nthe language requiring passengers in taxis and for-hire vehicles to wear\nsafety belts.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNo negative impact to state anticipated.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nNovember 1 next succeeding the date on which it shall become law, and\none year after taking effect for the signage requirement.\n",
